-- chem/netpiece.hypercubical — the charges' part of the energy on a closed piece of the diamond net, by solving Kirchhoff's
-- equations over the rationals (chem/vertex.hypercubical's `rref`), where chem/charge.hypercubical's tree counts are too many to
-- count one by one. The diamond net has two kinds of vertices; A at r is joined to B at r and at r less each of three
-- steps. Closed on itself with period two in each step it has sixteen vertices (A at r = 0 … 7 read as three bits,
-- B at 8 + r) and thirty-two lines, and is the four-dimensional cube's graph. `np-resistance n ls a b` is φ_a − φ_b
-- for the potential φ with unit current in at a and out at b. Checked (`np-cube`): from a vertex, the four
-- neighbours are at 15/32 (Foster's (n − 1)/m of chem/fluxsplit.hypercubical), the six at two lines at 7/12, the four at
-- three lines at 61/96, the one at four lines at 2/3, in units of one line; the string there is 1, 2, 3, 4. And the
-- solver against the tree counts on the cage (`np-cage`). A leaf: no module imports it.
import "fluxsplit.hypercubical"
import "vertex.hypercubical"

